@format 1
@id media-loading.in-audio-tab
@title In Audio tab
@section Media loading
@area In Audio tab
@entry audio-path-change, audio-items-add
@summary Show Audio-specific behavior for PListPathChange and the later PListItemsAdd notification, including the conditional current-plan save and immediate restore that occur before the requested media commits.
@related media-loading.common.docket-insertion, media-loading.common.files-selection, media-loading.common.viewer-gate, media-loading.common.media-publication
@tag media
@tag loading
@tag audio

@alias audio = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PAudioTab
@alias viewer = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PViewer

[audio-path-change] Audio Files current-path event <input>
= PListPathChange synchronously delivered a current path to PAudioPathShow.
> audio-path-result

[audio-items-add] Audio newly-added-items event <input>
= After the first-new-path PListPathChange handler returned, PListDocketAddHandle invoked PListItemsAdd with all newly added docket entries.
> audio-items-result

[audio-path-result] Audio selected-path adapter <decision>
- Ignore blank paths; for a nonblank path, PAudioPathShow first calls PAudioPlanSave before requesting the new source @ audio.PAudioPathShow(...)
? "Nonblank current path" > audio-save-gate
? "Blank current path" > audio-no-request

[audio-save-gate] Current Audio plan needs saving <decision>
- PAudioPlanSave returns without writing while plan loading is active, when no viewer source is currently committed, when that source is locked, or when the current plan is inactive and no saved plan already exists; otherwise it saves the current plan @ audio.PAudioPlanSave(...)
? "Save conditions met" > audio-save
? "Save skipped" > audio-save-skipped

[audio-save] Save current committed source plan <process>
- Save the current Audio work plan for the committed viewer source and update persistent carried Audio state @ audio.PAudioPlanSave(...)
> audio-save-join

[audio-save-skipped] Current-plan write skipped <junction>
> audio-save-join

[audio-save-join] Audio pre-request save paths converge <junction>
> audio-viewer-call

[audio-items-result] Persistent Audio carry active <decision>
- PAudioItemsHandle returns when plan loading is active or Audio persistent mode is off; otherwise it reads the carried Audio plan for new entries @ audio.PAudioItemsHandle(...)
? "Persistent carry applies" > audio-items-save
? "No persistent carry" > audio-items-nochange

[audio-viewer-call] Call shared viewer request synchronously <process>
- Call PViewerSourceOpen for the requested path; the Common / Viewer gate behavior occurs during this call and any backend work continues asynchronously after it returns @ audio.PAudioPathShow(...)
  @ viewer.PViewerSourceOpen(...)
> immediate-restore

[audio-no-request] Audio viewer request omitted <output>
= Audio does not call PAudioPlanSave or PViewerSourceOpen.

[audio-items-save] Save carried plan for each new entry <process>
- For every added entry, read any source-specific Audio plan, resolve it against the persistent carried plan, and save the resolved plan @ audio.PAudioItemsHandle(...)
> audio-items-saved

[audio-items-nochange] Added-items handler makes no plan changes <output>
= Newly added paths receive no Audio plan write from PAudioItemsHandle.

[immediate-restore] Restore using currently committed viewer source <process>
- Immediately after PViewerSourceOpen returns, call PAudioPlanRestore; it reads PViewerSourcePath and duration from the viewer, which are not changed to the requested source until a later successful viewer commit @ audio.PAudioPlanRestore(...)
  @ property viewer.PViewerSourcePath
- Apply the resolved plan/skip state and reopen/update the Audio monitor using that currently committed viewer source and duration @ audio.PAudioPlanRestore(...)
! On a normal asynchronous new-source request this means restoration usually uses the previous committed source, or null on an initially empty viewer. Audio has no PViewerMediaChange subscription that automatically reruns PAudioPlanRestore after the new media later commits.
> audio-transition-complete

[audio-items-saved] Added Audio plans synchronized <output>
= Persistent Audio state has been resolved and saved for every newly added item.

[audio-transition-complete] Immediate Audio transition finished <output>
= PAudioPathShow has returned while the requested media load may still be running independently; the immediate plan/monitor state is based on the viewer state that existed at restore time.
